completed_at: "2026-09-03T08:52:40.000Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "The original before_hash and after_hash of every re-anchored entry are retained durably, so a verifier can reconstruct the pre-re-anchor anchor set without holding the pre-merge stream; A verification path confirms that a re-anchor changed only anchors and entry ordering, and did not change any author, timestamp, operation, message or patch content, and fails loudly when it did; The lenient patch-repair path records the original patch operations it replaced or skipped, not only an aggregate skippedOps count, so recorded intent survives a repair; The same retention applies to every path that re-anchors - merge, history-repair, history-redact and history-compact - enforced once at the shared pipeline rather than per command, which makes pm-34w8za a natural carrier; History compaction states explicitly what it can no longer prove after pruning a checkpointed prefix, so the loss is recorded rather than silent; A negative-control test tampers with one entry's author or patch inside a simulated merge window and proves the verification path rejects the resulting stream, since a check that cannot fail adds no assurance"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: 94
resolution: "Centralized rewrite resealing and prior-envelope evidence across merge, repair, redaction, compaction, and provenance normalization; retained replaced patches or digests; added compaction stream proofs; refused exact stale runtime pins for mutation while preserving reads and an explicit override."
expected_result: "A third party can verify rewritten history ancestry and detect content tampering, with explicit limitations after redaction or prefix pruning."
actual_result: "Rewrite evidence reconstructs prior anchors and record envelopes, tampering fails loudly, sensitive redaction retains digest-only proof, compaction states its limitation, stale exact pins refuse writes, and all linked/manual gates pass."
